    "turn_text": "I was a defensive guy. I never really called offensive play. So I stayed more on the defensive side of the ball to coach University of Miami back in the in glory days when Trent deal for beat me for opening game when you're they won the he won the Heisman Trophy. But that being said, You do most of your work in the summer. The thing about football is you can go back and look at films, you can make game plans for every game that you're getting ready to play against your opponents. Now, then you're going to get two or three films from that opponent for that year. They're a little bit different personnel, look how they changed. But almost everything's called and scripted before the game starts. Depending on down and distance, short yardage, long yardage, personal hill you put in the game, who they throw it to, what they like to do. You play all the percentages. There's no guesswork in it. There's some people, Spurrier was a good friend of mine and he shot me up all the time. He's a good",
